<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04X4">Remark <span data-tag="04X4">10.2.3.3</span>.</a> In the situation of Definition <a data-tag="04X2" href="/tag/04X2">10.2.3.1</a>, $Y_0$ is an image of $f$ if and only if there exists a $2$-simplex </p>
<div class="equation" id="04X5">
<span class="equation-label"><a data-tag="04X5" href="/tag/04X5">10.22</a></span>
<div>\begin{equation}  \begin{gathered}\label{equation:image-in-infinity} \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ &amp;  Y_0 \ar [dr]^{i} &amp;  \\ X \ar [ur]^{q} \ar [rr]^{f} &amp;  &amp;  Y } \end{gathered} \end{equation}</div>
</div>
<p> in the $\infty $-category $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$, where $q$ is a quotient morphism. If this condition is satisfied, we say that the $2$-simplex (<a data-tag="04X5" href="/tag/04X5">10.22</a>) <em>exhibits $Y_0$ as an image of $f$</em>. </p>
